-- title:
--   Integrality of an element from integrality of its q-expansion
-- statement:
--   Let $R$, $R'$ and $L$ be commutative rings with $R'$ noetherian local and $L$ an $R$-algebra whose structure map $R \to L$ is injective. Let $\iota\colon R \to R'$ and $\pi\colon R' \to R$ be ring homomorphisms with $\pi \circ \iota = \mathrm{id}_R$, and let $t \in R'$ satisfy $\pi(t) = 0$, $t \in \mathfrak{m}_{R'}$, and $\ker \pi \subseteq (t) + (\ker \pi)^2$. Let $e\colon R' \to L[[q]]$ be a ring homomorphism such that $e(\iota(r))$ is the constant power series with value $r$ in $L$ for every $r \in R$, and such that $e(i)$ has vanishing constant coefficient for every $i \in \ker \pi$. Assume $e(t)$ is the image under $L[[q]] \leftarrow R[[q]]$ (coefficientwise application of $R \to L$) of some $u \in R[[q]]$ whose coefficient of $q^1$ is a unit of $R$. Then for every ideal $\mathfrak{a} \subseteq R$, every $z \in R'$ and every $P \in R[[q]]$ with $e(z)$ equal to the image of $P$ in $L[[q]]$ and all coefficients of $P$ lying in $\mathfrak{a}$, one has $z \in \mathfrak{a}R'$, the ideal of $R'$ generated by $\iota(\mathfrak{a})$.
--
--   This is the saturation step of the integral $q$-expansion principle in abstract form: a formal expansion map $e$ along a section, with parameter $t$ whose expansion has unit linear coefficient, detects membership in an extended ideal, the cases $\mathfrak{a} = 0$ and $\mathfrak{a} = (p)$ giving injectivity of $q$-expansion and $p$-integrality respectively. It is used in the comparison of germs at a cusp with power series expansions on a rational model of a modular curve.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_RingHom_mem_map_of_powerSeries_map_eq_of_forall_coeff_mem.lean

